 Product 1 vs demand | Main loss | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 7 | every 2 days | 420 (+10%) | 574 (+5%) | almost none, reasonable buffer | best |\n| 3 | every 2 days | 382 (≈0%) | 548 (≈0%) | random shortages, no buffer | good |\n| 2 | product 0 every 4 days, product 1 every 2 | 418 | 574 | extra product 0 holding, about −110 | good |\n| 4 | every 3 days | 408 | 583 | rhythm costs ≈ −90, plus a longer stretch between deliveries and space near 148 | borderline |\n| 0 | every 2 days | 473 (+24%) | 574 | product 0 piles up, about 7 units per cycle written off, ≈ −400 to −600 | below |\n| 1 | daily | +5% | +5% | ≈ 26 × 46 order fees, ≈ −370 | below |\n| 6 | every 2 days | +24% | 678 (+24%) | write-offs and holding on both products | bad |\n| 5 | every 4 days | — | — | batches of 166 units, warehouse overflow, high product 1 holding | bad |\n\n**Stability under random demand.** Candidate 7 has a buffer, so it handles demand swings best. Candidate 3 has none, so a run of high-demand days brings penalties. Candidate 4's longer gap between deliveries adds more uncertainty than the 2-day rhythm."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5054, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5054}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T09:00:10.679Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWFeELZ2FXi47d8hFEU3"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01JjcW4DoBhwQN1vLTSpFo11", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"t